{"name": "Zhiyuan Cao", "institution": "Yale University", "department": "Computational Biology and Biomedical Informatics", "title_on_roster": "", "roster_url": "https://cbb.yale.edu/people", "profile_url": "https://medicine.yale.edu/profile/hua-xu/", "filter": "all", "ai_venues": null, "first_paper": null, "heritage": "chinese", "position_class": "other", "position": {"value": "", "evidence": {"source_url": "https://cbb.yale.edu/people", "quote": "Zhiyuan Cao - Xu lab - Chen lab", "checked_on": "2026-10-30"}}, "email": null, "homepage": null, "lab_website": null, "google_scholar": null, "cv": null, "pubs": null, "contact": null, "research": {"text": "Dr. Hua Xu is Robert T. McCluskey Professor and Vice Chair for Research and Development, Department of Biomedical Informatics and Data Science at Yale School of Medicine (YSM). He also serves as Associate Dean for Biomedical Informatics at YSM. He received his Ph.D. in Biomedical Informatics from Columbia University. His primary research interests include biomedical natural language processing (NLP), large language models (LLMs), and AI agents, as well as their applications in clinical practice and biomedical research. His research is funded by multiple agencies (i.e., NLM, NCI, NIGMS, NIA, AHA, and CPRIT), and methods/tools developed in his lab have been widely used to support diverse biomedical applications. Dr. Xu is a fellow of both the American College of Medical Informatics (ACMI) and the International Academy of Health Sciences Informatics (IAHSI). See more information about Dr. X", "source_url": "https://medicine.yale.edu/profile/hua-xu/"}, "recruiting": [], "start": [], "papers": [], "problems": ["papers: deferred"]}
{"name": "Kexing Li", "institution": "Yale University", "department": "Computational Biology and Biomedical Informatics", "title_on_roster": "", "roster_url": "https://cbb.yale.edu/people", "profile_url": "https://ysph.yale.edu/profile/jeffrey-townsend/", "filter": "all", "ai_venues": null, "first_paper": null, "heritage": "chinese", "position_class": "teaching", "position": {"value": "Lecturer in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence", "evidence": {"source_url": "https://ysph.yale.edu/profile/jeffrey-townsend/", "quote": "e Now Contact Careers at YSPH Faculty Open Positions Senior Lecturer in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in Public Health Department Chair - Department of Envi", "checked_on": "2026-10-30"}}, "email": null, "homepage": null, "lab_website": null, "google_scholar": null, "cv": null, "pubs": null, "contact": null, "research": {"text": "", "source_url": null}, "recruiting": [], "start": [], "papers": [], "problems": ["skipped: senior title on profile (Lecturer in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence)"]}
{"name": "Zhaochen Ye", "institution": "Yale University", "department": "Computational Biology and Biomedical Informatics", "title_on_roster": "", "roster_url": "https://cbb.yale.edu/people", "profile_url": "https://medicine.yale.edu/profile/david-braun/", "filter": "all", "ai_venues": null, "first_paper": null, "heritage": "chinese", "position_class": "other", "position": {"value": "", "evidence": {"source_url": "https://cbb.yale.edu/people", "quote": "Zhaochen Ye - Braun lab - Kleinstein lab", "checked_on": "2026-10-30"}}, "email": null, "homepage": null, "lab_website": "https://www.thebraunlab.org/", "google_scholar": null, "cv": null, "pubs": null, "contact": null, "research": {"text": "What are the local (tumor microenvironment), regional, and systemic determinants of anti-tumor immunity? The tumor-immune microenvironment is comprised of heterogeneous cell types that may positively or negatively impact anti-tumor immune responses. Our work identified key immune cell populations and cellular interaction circuits that were enriched in advanced clear cell kidney cancer (see Braun*, Street* et al, Cancer Cell , 2021 ), and defined the immune microenvironment of rare variants (chromophobe kidney cancer, see Labaki et al, Journal of Clinical Oncology , 2025 ). We now aim to utilize single-cell proteogenomic tools to systematically dissect this complex ecosystem and identify candidate immune cell populations and cellular states that impact response or resistance to immune checkpoint inhibitors ( Hugaboom*, Wirth*, Street*, Ruthen* et al, Cancer Discovery , 2025 ). Further, we", "source_url": "https://medicine.yale.edu/profile/david-braun/"}, "recruiting": [], "start": [], "papers": [], "problems": ["papers: deferred"]}
{"name": "Haley Xiaohe Zhang", "institution": "Yale University", "department": "Computational Biology and Biomedical Informatics", "title_on_roster": "", "roster_url": "https://cbb.yale.edu/people", "profile_url": "https://medicine.yale.edu/profile/joel-gelernter/", "filter": "all", "ai_venues": null, "first_paper": null, "heritage": "chinese", "position_class": "other", "position": {"value": "", "evidence": {"source_url": "https://cbb.yale.edu/people", "quote": "Haley Xiaohe Zhang - Gelernter lab - Xu lab", "checked_on": "2026-10-30"}}, "email": null, "homepage": null, "lab_website": null, "google_scholar": null, "cv": null, "pubs": null, "contact": null, "research": {"text": "The research focus of his laboratory is genetics of psychiatric illness – phenotypes including cocaine, opioid, nicotine, cannabis, and alcohol use and use disorder, posttraumatic stress disorder (PTSD), depression, and panic and other anxiety disorders. He also studies a range of related phenotypes, including pharmacogenomics; other complex traits; and basic issues in population and complex trait genetics. The overall approach involves study of genetic polymorphism and sequence variation, on a molecular level and from the perspective of population genetics. Dr Gelernter’s laboratory published genomewide association studies (GWAS) and other downstream analyses for cannabis use and use disorder, opioid use disorder, PTSD and related traits, alcohol use disorder and problematic alcohol use, and other psychiatric and medical traits - such as level of physical activity, and how exercise rela", "source_url": "https://medicine.yale.edu/profile/joel-gelernter/"}, "recruiting": [], "start": [], "papers": [], "problems": ["papers: deferred"]}
